%% AI PR Reviewer - System Architecture Diagram
%% This diagram shows the complete flow from GitHub PR events to AI-powered reviews

sequenceDiagram
    participant User as Developer
    participant GitHub as GitHub Repository
    participant Actions as GitHub Actions Runner
    participant Main as Main Controller
    participant Options as Options Parser
    participant Bot as AI Bot Factory
    participant LightBot as Light Bot (GPT-3.5)
    participant HeavyBot as Heavy Bot (GPT-4)
    participant Review as Review Engine
    participant Diff as Diff Parser
    participant Files as File Processor
    participant Prompts as Prompt Templates
    participant Commenter as Comment Manager
    participant API as GitHub API

    %% Initial PR Event
    User->>GitHub: Creates/Updates Pull Request
    GitHub->>Actions: Triggers workflow (pull_request_target)
    Actions->>Main: Executes main.ts entry point
    
    %% Initialization Phase
    Main->>Options: Parse configuration & environment
    Options-->>Main: Validated options & path filters
    Main->>Bot: Create dual bot instances
    Bot->>LightBot: Initialize GPT-3.5 for summaries
    Bot->>HeavyBot: Initialize GPT-4 for reviews
    Bot-->>Main: Bot instances ready
    
    %% Review Process Initiation
    Main->>Review: Start codeReview() pipeline
    Review->>GitHub: Fetch PR metadata & context
    GitHub-->>Review: PR title, description, commits
    Review->>API: Get incremental diff (base to head)
    API-->>Review: File changes & patches
    
    %% File Processing Phase
    Review->>Files: Filter & process changed files
    Files->>Options: Apply path filters
    Options-->>Files: Filtered file list
    Files->>API: Fetch file contents for context
    API-->>Files: File content & metadata
    Files->>Diff: Split patches into reviewable chunks
    Diff-->>Files: Structured patch data
    Files-->>Review: Processed files ready for analysis
    
    %% Summarization Phase
    loop For each file
        Review->>Prompts: Render summarization template
        Prompts-->>Review: Formatted prompt with context
        Review->>LightBot: Request file summary
        LightBot->>LightBot: Analyze changes & classify
        LightBot-->>Review: Summary + triage (NEEDS_REVIEW/APPROVED)
    end
    
    %% Batch Summary Processing
    Review->>Prompts: Render changeset summary template
    Prompts-->>Review: Batch summary prompt
    Review->>HeavyBot: Consolidate file summaries
    HeavyBot-->>Review: Consolidated summary
    
    %% Detailed Review Phase
    loop For files marked NEEDS_REVIEW
        Review->>Prompts: Render detailed review template
        Prompts-->>Review: Review prompt with code context
        Review->>HeavyBot: Request detailed code review
        HeavyBot->>HeavyBot: Analyze code quality & suggest improvements
        HeavyBot-->>Review: Line-by-line review comments
        Review->>Commenter: Buffer review comments
    end
    
    %% Comment Generation & Posting
    Review->>Prompts: Render final summary template
    Prompts-->>Review: Summary prompt
    Review->>HeavyBot: Generate PR summary
    HeavyBot-->>Review: Final PR summary
    Review->>Commenter: Prepare all comments for posting
    Commenter->>API: Create PR review with comments
    API->>GitHub: Post review & line comments
    GitHub-->>User: Notify of review completion
    
    %% Interactive Chat Phase (Separate Event)
    Note over User,API: Interactive Chat Mode
    User->>GitHub: Mentions @coderabbitai in comment
    GitHub->>Actions: Triggers pull_request_review_comment event
    Actions->>Main: Execute review comment handler
    Main->>Review: Process chat request
    Review->>Commenter: Get conversation context
    Commenter->>API: Fetch comment chain & diff context
    API-->>Commenter: Comment history & file context
    Commenter-->>Review: Conversation context
    Review->>Prompts: Render chat response template
    Prompts-->>Review: Chat prompt with full context
    Review->>HeavyBot: Generate contextual response
    HeavyBot-->>Review: AI response
    Review->>Commenter: Format reply comment
    Commenter->>API: Post reply to conversation
    API->>GitHub: Update comment thread
    GitHub-->>User: Notify of AI response

    %% Error Handling & Retry Logic
    Note over LightBot,HeavyBot: Built-in retry logic for API failures
    Note over Commenter,API: Rate limiting & throttling protection
    Note over Review: Token limit validation before API calls
    Note over Options: Path filtering prevents processing unwanted files